; 42-hint.kurt

; `hint` is a toggle (`hint on` / `hint off`), meant to make Kurt print a
; hint for what might come next before each prompt, in the interactive
; shell.  As of this writing it is a planned feature: the switch exists and
; can be flipped, but nothing reads it yet -- so, unlike the
; other toggles in this section (`verbose`, `indent`, `calc`), you won't see
; any difference in behaviour from using it today.

hint                ; reports the current setting ("hint off")
hint on
hint                ; ("hint on")
hint off
